<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eadberht Præn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 796–798</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Eadberht III of Kent</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eadberht Præn was king of Kent from 796 to 798, leading a revolt against Mercian rule after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa</a>. A former cleric, he seized the throne and drove out Archbishop Æthelheard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>, but in 798 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coenwulf-of-mercia">Coenwulf of Mercia</a> invaded Kent, captured him, had him blinded and his hands cut off, and restored Mercian control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eadberht-praen.jpg" alt="Eadberht Præn" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eadberht_Praen_Coin_of_Kent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
